CM_ BO_ 2376073411 "Front-board acceleration timer command. Send this extended frame to 0x0DA000C3 for DBF: command 0 disables the timer, 1 clears prior results and arms the timer, and 2 clears results while preserving the current enabled state.";
CM_ BO_ 2376597504 "Front-board acceleration timer result/status. After enable, the first FL or FR wheel-speed pulse starts timing. The timer uses a 17.66 in front tire diameter, 16 wheel-speed pulses per revolution, and a 246 ft target. Completion bits indicate valid FL-only, FR-only, and averaged-wheel elapsed times in milliseconds.";
CM_ BO_ 2376601600 "Front-board acceleration timer live distance. Distances use the 17.66 in front tire diameter and 16 wheel-speed pulses per revolution. FL, FR, and averaged front-wheel distances are reported in feet while the timer is armed/running and hold their final values after completion.";
CM_ BO_ 2376073412 "Front-board manual lap timer command. Send this extended frame to 0x0DA000C4 for DBF: command 0 resets the timer to idle and clears all laps, 1 starts the timer from idle or resumes from pause, 2 records the current lap split and begins the next lap, and 3 pauses the timer. The timer is controlled entirely over CAN and uses no sensors.";
CM_ BO_ 2376794112 "Front-board manual lap timer results, multiplexed by DBF_Lap_Timer_Lap_Index (0-39 selects lap number index+1). DBF_Lap_Timer_Lap_Count (completed laps), DBF_Lap_Timer_State, and DBF_Lap_Timer_Current_Lap (live in-progress lap time) are present in every frame. Recorded and live lap times use 10 ms resolution and saturate at 655.35 s. Up to 40 laps are supported.";